Podroid migration scripts.

The immutable lower squashfs contains an explicit `index` with one canonical
versionCode per line in strictly increasing order. podroid-migrate validates the
entire bounded index, then runs indexed <version>.sh hooks for:
  applied-version < version <= system-version
The marker advances atomically only after all selected hooks succeed.

Rules:
  - Add the versionCode to `index` and add <versionCode>.sh in the same change.
  - Keep index entries digits-only, unique, and strictly increasing.
  - Scripts MUST be idempotent because a crash re-runs the current migration.
  - Scripts execute only from /mnt/lower; never execute copied-up /etc content.
  - Do not delete workload or user data. Restrict imperative fixups to reviewed
    system-layer paths and use the no-follow helper for filesystem mutation.
